      "why": "k chained micro-rotations/cycle raises throughput but duplicates shifters/adders, so it should be strictly larger in area than iterative for the same accuracy. Included with a modest share to verify it does not offer a cheaper area point (e.g. small k with small W) and to cover any front segment where extra throughput is traded for area. k kept small (2..4) since larger k only inflates area with no benefit given the loose throughput floor.",
